{"title":"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three players, Ava, Beau, and Cato, are playing a tournament. Each person plays exactly two games, one game against each of the other players. If a game ends in a tie, both players are awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. Otherwise, the winning player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> points and the losing player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p>For example, if the tournament results are as shown below and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129a394e53ae5d9485467a5da722ed2d61c63077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 2$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then points are awarded as follows:\n</p><p>(add a table to the Problem 2 page)\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the sum of the points that have been awarded to the three players when the tournament has finished. In the example above, Ava is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point, Beau is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and Cato is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae948412b3206828fd197dbd41fd8a41bf7c4de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> in the example.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the tournament results are as follows: Ava and Beau tie, Beau loses to Cato, Ava and Cato tie. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de876fde34b19dde31df3ef3df1a098091a61e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>According to the tournament rules, if both Ava and Beau tie, then they are each awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. This means that there is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34a068fc593714a83c298e0e3570977270c1c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> points so far.\n</p><p>Next, if Beau loses to Cato, Cato is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de876fde34b19dde31df3ef3df1a098091a61e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> points and Beau is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points. This means that there is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18ff05f5dd2358a1db7b6e94357de4175e0da3c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 + 0 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> points so far.\n</p><p>Finally, if Ava and Cato tie, then they are each awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. This means that there is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30a0862813e16de39b718854caa8b1c77f9d2c66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 1 \\times 2 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> so far.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a719d96a739c9e69136be4201afa92c56cc9e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {S = 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"59\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018031917\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 71/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1050/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3294/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.329      1 2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   17.329      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35024:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018031917 and revision id 271948. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}